  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The length of a rectangle is 4 cm greater than its width. If its area is $96\\text{ cm}^2$, find the length of the rectangle.\n\nUse a quadratic equation and clearly define any pronumeral introduced into your solution.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$12\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "Let $x$ cm be the width. The length is $(x+4)$ cm.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+4)&=96\\\\x^2+4x-96&=0\\\\(x-8)(x+12)&=0\\\\x&=8\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=-12\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe width must be positive, so $x=8$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Length}&=8+4\\\\\\text{Length}&=12\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
